moviegoers of all ages probably  recognize joe pesci from his streetwise  fast talking performances in films like  goodfellas and home alone pesci has  stayed mostly out of the spotlight since  the turn of the millennium but that  doesn't mean he's disappeared entirely  here's the untold truth of joe pesci  born joseph frank pesci on february 9  1943 in newark new jersey joe pesci was  thrown into the spotlight at an early  age by his father angelo who saw show  business as a ticket to giving his  family a better life by the time he was  five years old pesci made his debut on  star time kids a television variety  series that aired from 1950 to 1955. the  experience was by pesci's own  description less than pleasurable in a  1992 interview with the new york times  he said my father loved me so much that  he did not want me to be a laborer or  anything i don't know if it's the right  thing to do push your kids into  something and then stay on them until  they do it let them pick what they want  to do  though pesci was less than enthused  about performing it kept him afloat  during his pre-famed days pesci sang and  played guitar in a string of pop and  rock acts most notably in the touring  version of the popular new york act joey  d and the starlighters which provided  him with his first feature film  appearance as an extra in the band's  star vehicle hey let's twist pesci then  made his bid for pop stardom in 1968  with the release of his first solo album  little joe short can sing but the lp  wasn't a hit so he returned to gigging  alongside another jersey musician frank  vincent however live club music had  fallen out of fashion by the early 70s  so the pair turned to comedy forming the  duo vincent and pesci i'm funny how i  mean funny like i'm a clown i am use you  i make you laugh decades after they hung  up the act vincent would remain pesci's  friend off camera and frequent nemesis  on film pesci brutalized vincent in  raging bull and beat him to death in  goodfellas while vincent returned the  favor by bashing in pesci's skull and  casino  in 1976 heshi had his first credited  movie role in family enforcer also known  as the death collector a low-budget  mafia thriller starring pesci and joe  cortese as muscle for the mob solid  reviews prompted pesci to head to  hollywood but a lack of further success  sent him packing back to the bronx where  he worked as a restaurant manager it was  at this low point that martin scorsese  and robert de niro came calling the  director and star had seen pesci and  family enforcer and sought him out for  their next project the boxing drama  raging bull heshi played joe lamotta the  brother manager and eventual enemy of  short-tempered boxer jake lamotta which  earned him a nomination for best  supporting actor at the oscars the  following year and made his name one to  remember from 1980 to 1998 heshi lent  his unique charm to a handful of iconic  movies from scorsese collaborations such  as goodfellas and casino to comedies  like home alone and my cousin vinnie he  had a small part opposite de niro in the  legendary sergio leone's last film once  upon a time in america portrayed  real-life pilot david ferry and jfk and  had a recurring role as leo goetz in the  lethal weapon franchise however many of  pesci's credits are likely to be total  obscurities to even the most seasoned  moviegoers for instance in 1983 pesci  starred as a bowling alley owner with  dreams of stardom in the west german  musical dear mr wonderful it's also  likely that you miss pesci as the uncle  of the bride in betsy's wedding or his  thinly veiled take on legendary  photographer ouija in the public eye  the takeaway peshi's hits are very big  but his misses disappear with little in  between  pesci has given few interviews since  announcing his retirement so his reasons  for the decision remain solely with him  however it's possible that he simply  lost his taste for the projects that  were being offered to him as far back as  1992 pesci told the new york times that  many of the roles brought to him were  quote stupid ethnic italian parts with  pizza pie stupid jokes while he mostly  avoided that characterization in his  film work pesci did withstand a barrage  of jokes about his height in the dismal  nbc action comedy half nelson heschi was  top billed as rocky nelson an nypd  detective who works for a private  security firm while trying to launch an  acting career the series co-created by  glen a larson paired pesci with saturday  night live alum victoria jackson as a  scattered brain secretary former  football player fred williamson as  rocky's boss and a visibly unwell dean  martin as himself at the time of its  release critic david handler described  half nelson as quote managing to leave  you feeling both bored and soiled which  undoubtedly helped capsize the series  after just seven episodes  joe pesci's oscar win for his portrayal  of gangster tommy devito and goodfellas  helped to wipe away any residue from  half nelson or his other early  obscurities and it's likely that he saw  his win as the start of a new and  improved phase of his career he told the  new york times i love to star in movies  but i want to have good roles it doesn't  help to get starring roles in something  that's no good i mean that will just  kill you although he netted several box  office hits much of his output during  the 1990s was dismissed by critics and  audiences alike attempts to fashion  pesci into a comedic leading man in the  super and go on fishing robust as was  his attempt at tugging heartstrings in  the terminally soggy with honors which  cast him as a homeless man with a big  heart and a scholar's brain by 1998  pesci had clearly lost his patience with  the industry after logging his third and  final turn as machine gun mouthed leo  goetz in lethal weapon 4 which earned  him a razzy nomination he retired from  acting as a full-time profession and  focused his energies elsewhere  okay come on whatever with several  notable exceptions pesci mostly stuck to  his decision to put acting on the back  burner instead he focused his energy on  golf and to the surprise of many went  back to singing in 1998 pesci released  his second album vincent laguardia  gambini sings just for you named for his  character and my cousin vinnie despite  his ill-advised past at hip-hop with the  infamous single wise guy pesci still  proved his musical powers with  renditions of what a wonderful world and  the ray charles number i've got news for  you although critics and listeners alike  largely dismissed the album as a vanity  project pesci kept his hand in music as  joe dogs he earned respectable reviews  for falling in love again a  collaboration with jazz organist joey  defrancesco and held his own alongside  his one-time idol little jimmy scott on  the folks who live on the hill a duet  featured on the legendary vocalists  final studio album i go back home two  years later pesci released his third  album still singing which featured two  duets with maroon 5's adam levine  in a 2016 interview comedy legend don  rickles who appeared with pesci in  casino said of his co-star i think  sometimes he believed he was with the  mob but he got over it given pesci's  multitude of terrifying gangster  performances it's understandable how  some might misconstrue him as a maid man  in the real world while there are tales  of the actor interacting with career  criminals pesci has kept himself out of  trouble off-screen well mostly in 2006  pesci was involved in an alleged assault  against an overzealous fan in florida  according to a police report pesci  struck a man who ignored his request to  refrain from taking his picture but  prosecutors dismissed the allegations  over a lack of evidence a half decade  later pesci was involved in not one but  two legal cases the first in 2012  involved his ex-wife actress claudia  harrow who was sentenced to 12 years for  allegedly hiring a hitman to whack her  second husband stuntman garrett warren  pesci was briefly considered as the  supposed source of financing for the  failed hit though the allegations were  eventually dismissed the following year  pesci was awarded an unspecified court  settlement from fiore pictures after he  sued the company for allegedly reducing  his salary and role in what would become  the infamous 2018 biopic gotti with john  travolta there's no question that joe  pesci is a complicated individual even  he's noted as much in an interview with  the baltimore sun he recalled having an  existential crisis while playing a game  of golf saying i didn't know who the  hell was about to hit that golf ball was  it leo goetz or david ferry or tommy or  harry or joe i spent so much time as  somebody else and so little time is  myself i lost sight of who i was for an  instant pesci is an enormously talented  actor and if his quietly menacing  performance and the irishman is any  indication one's still capable of  mesmerizing audiences well into his 70s  however he seems to prefer to focus on  other outlets that appear to have a  greater hold on his heart including  singing and tending to his own personal  well-being if acting has left him  feeling misunderstood misrepresented and  even unsure of who he really is it's  hard to blame him for choosing to step  away from it  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite actors are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

